# Local decision protocol

This file is the operational contract delivered with the package. It is sufficient to maintain decisions without consulting the source kit.

## Source of truth

- Living truth lives only in `_app-vault/docs/decisions/`.
- One file per product domain, in `kebab-case`.
- `_app-vault/INDEX.md` is a map: it points to files and derives `## By feature` from `Affects:`; it never copies values.
- `_app-vault/specs/` is technical context, not a rule source.
- `.app-work/` is process and is never a decision input.

## Canonical form

Each rule has its own heading:

```markdown
### DEC-001 — Rule name

Living statement of the rule.
```

`Affects: [feature-a, feature-b]` goes right after the domain title. Features use `kebab-case` slugs from the `INDEX.md` vocabulary.

## Identity and numbering

- `DEC-NNN` is the rule's stable identity, not of the current text or value.
- Before creating, inventory every file in `docs/decisions/`, counting live headings and IDs in `## History`; the maximum is per project, not per domain. An empty inventory starts at `DEC-001`.
- Use `max + 1`; never reuse a removed ID and never renumber an existing decision.
- To match a source without an ID, compare domain, subject/object, condition/scope, and rule type with variable values removed. If two candidates are equally plausible, stop and ask for confirmation.

## Change, addition, and removal

- Before contradicting a living rule, present the previous value, source, new value, and other affected dependencies; obtain applicable human confirmation. Only then, if the value changes, change the statement under the same `DEC-NNN` and append a note right below: `_Changed YYYY-MM-DD — was: <old value>. Reason: <reason>._`
- New notes go above old ones; keep at most about three.
- An addition without contradiction creates a new `DEC-NNN`, with no change note. A new domain or feature requires updating `## Domains`, the feature vocabulary, and `## By feature` in `INDEX.md`; derive the index from the `Affects:` fields in the same write.
- Removal is rare: first, search for pending citations across the whole repository, including `.app-work/`. Pending citations must be resolved before removal; search with `rg --hidden` or explicit paths, since `.app-work/` is hidden. After authorization, remove the clause and append to `## History`: `- YYYY-MM-DD — DEC-NNN removed. Was: <old rule>. Reason: <reason>.` That ID must not remain as a live clause and must not be reused.
- A rule reaching more than one domain updates every affected file and cites the sibling decisions in the notes.

## Human promotion

Text in a guide, brainstorm, PRD, or ledger is a process candidate, not a rule. Only materialize a decision when the user explicitly confirms the candidate, its statement, domain, and origin evidence. Without confirmation, keep it as a candidate and do not use it to govern the product.

## Territory split

The user-observable effect goes to `docs/decisions/`. The implementation norm goes to `project-rules/` and references the `DEC-NNN`; do not copy the same literal value in both territories.
